 "format": "Commander",
 "name": "Gandalf the Grey: Izzet Wizards",
 "notes": [
  "Nov 24, 2026 (final for tonight): Glamdring back in for Shock — they'd rather have the sword. Shock goes back to the bulk box.",
  "Nov 24, 2026 (sleeving tonight, part 2): Faithless Looting from the house in for Red Mage's Rapier (one more cheap spell for Gandalf).",
  "Nov 24, 2026 (sleeving tonight): bulk found at home goes in — Fact or Fiction (for Jace's Ingenuity), Arcane Denial (for Spellshift), Negate (for Blue Elemental Blast), Muddle the Mixture (for Jace's Ruse), Big Score (for Elemental Summoning), Shock (for Glamdring). Bilbo, Retired Burglar is locked in every version at his request (\"The Goat\").",
  "Nov 24, 2026 (later still): Mana Geyser back in for Illusion Spinners — at a 4-player table it makes a pile of red mana for Grapeshot, Fiery Confluence or Expansion // Explosion. Kept in all three upgraded versions too.",
  "Nov 24, 2026 (later): sleeved Sol Ring (for Mana Geyser, which then came back), Arcane Signet (for Mind Stone), Command Tower (for an Island) and Lightning Bolt (for Ranger's Firebrand) from the house. Wizard's Rockets stays for now.",
  "Nov 24, 2026: main list replaced with his newly sleeved 100 (146-card pile: 19 duplicates removed, then 27 cuts — 3 Island, 2 Mountain, Wizards of the _____, Shivan Dragon, Artisan of Forms, Captain of the Mists, Havengul Runebinder, Izzet Guildmage, Jalira, Kheru Spellsnatcher, Meletis Charlatan, Mystic Archaeologist, Reckless Scholar, Sage of Mysteries, Shaper Apprentice, Watertrap Weaver, Bazaar Trademage, Ghitu Lavarunner, Viashino Pyromancer, Izzet Staticaster, Flame Rift, Browse, Mystic Speculation, Totally Lost). Old Stage 1–3, Spellslinger B2 and Max B2 versions replaced by three: Bang for the Buck, Ideal (B2), Ideal (B3).",
  "Gandalf triggers only on instants and sorceries, choosing a mode not yet chosen: tap or untap, 3 damage to each opponent (4 with Tomik), copy the spell, or put Gandalf on top of the library. Blinking him resets the modes.",
  "Middle kid's must-have: Electrostatic Infantry (in every upgraded version; first buy). Orko (Delina, Wild Mage) was considered: fun with Wizard enter effects, not a power upgrade; not added."
 ],
