   "label": "Bang for the Buck",
   "name": "Gandalf Izzet — Bang for the Buck",
   "notes": [
    "About $41 for 37 cards, every one under $4 (most under 50¢). Same shape as Ideal B2 with his own cards in the priciest slots: Consider the Prime Directive for Force of Negation, Sudden Setback for Swan Song, Mysidian Elder for Snapcaster Mage, Serum Visionary for Spellseeker, Balmor for Ral, Monsoon Mage, Ferrous Lake for Riverglide Pathway, basics for Otawara and Fiery Islet.",
    "Biggest gains per dollar, buy in this order: Electrostatic Infantry (his must-have), the 1-mana cantrips (Ponder, Preordain, Sleight of Hand, Serum Visions), Fire // Ice, Counterspell, then the cost reducers (Kaza, Stormcatch Mentor, Baral) and Veyran.",
    "32 lands + 4 rocks + 3 mana creatures + 4 cost reducers. 36 instants and sorceries (up from 26), 22 Wizards, plus Bilbo.",
    "Already sleeved (Nov 24): Sol Ring, Arcane Signet, Command Tower, Lightning Bolt, Fact or Fiction, Arcane Denial, Muddle the Mixture, Big Score, Faithless Looting. Check the house for Counterspell before buying; the collection isn't in mtg-data yet."
   ],
